# ROAST writes its outputs next to the subject MRI. A single run of the
# MNI152 example is ~650 MB, and three of its files exceed GitHub's 100 MB
# limit, so none of it belongs in the repository - it is all reproducible
# from the tracked inputs.

# 1. Anything carrying a run tag: <subject>_YYYYMMDDThhmmss[_suffix].<ext>
#    Matched on the tag rather than the extension, because a run emits .nii,
#    .mat, .msh, .pro, .pos and .pre, and getDP gains new ones over time.
example/*_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]T[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*

# 2. Derived images and segmentations, shared between runs of one subject:
#    <subject>_ras.nii and everything built from it (T1orT2 masks, seg8,
#    the _padded<N> and resampled variants, MNI-space copies).
example/*_ras.nii
example/*_ras_*
example/c[1-6]*.nii
example/*_seg8.mat
example/*_rmask.mat
example/*_roastLog

# 3. Error log written by runExamples.m and examples/run_examples.py
errLog.txt

# Octave MEX built from SPM12 source (see octave-compat/README.md)
lib/spm12/**/*.mex
lib/spm12/src/

# Example-suite scaffolding (see octave-compat/scripts/)
roast-suite-work/
master_cmds.json

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
